.TH KERN 1 "2025-01-01" "kern" "System Monitoring Tool"
.SH NAME
kern \- real-time system monitoring tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kern
[\-acdhmnv] [\-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR] [\-l \fILANG\fR] [\-r \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kern
is a comprehensive system monitoring tool that provides real-time information
about disk usage, CPU performance, memory utilization, and network statistics.
It features a colorful terminal interface with auto-refresh capabilities
and support for multiple languages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show all system information (default).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cpu
Show CPU information only.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-disk
Show disk information only.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mem
Show memory information only.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-net
Show network information only.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR
Set refresh interval in seconds (default: 2).
.TP
.B \-l \fILANG\fR
Set interface language. Supported languages: en, ru, zh, es, fr, de, ja, ko, it, pt, ar, hi, id, vi, th, tr, pl, nl, sv, da, no, fi, cs, hu, ro, bg, hr, sk, sl, et, lv, lt, uk, sr, bs, mk, sq, el, he, fa, ur, bn, ta, te, ml, kn, gu, mr, pa, ne, la, bo, ba, kk, mo, ka, hy, be, mn.
.TP
.B \-r \fIPORT\fR
Start remote API server on specified port.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B q
Quit the application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kern
Monitor all system resources with default settings.
.TP
.B kern \-d \-m
Monitor only disk and memory usage.
.TP
.B kern \-\-refresh=5 \-l ru
Update every 5 seconds with Russian interface.
.TP
.B kern \-r 26001
Start remote API server on port 26001.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kern/kern.json
Configuration file storing user preferences.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR htop (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR lscpu (1)
